Krita Nova 20 - Ctrl+T starts a transform right away

After a transform was applied (Enter) or cancelled (Esc), the Transform tool
stays active without a running transform, and pressing Ctrl+T again did
nothing: the transform only restarted after another click/tap on the canvas
(upstream bugs 343565, 375977). Switching to the tool from another tool
already started it immediately.

KisToolTransform::activate() now also listens to its own tool action
("KisToolTransform", Ctrl+T by default): when it is triggered while the tool
is active and no transform is running, a new transform starts at once, in the
last used mode - exactly what the click on the canvas did.

diff --git a/plugins/tools/tool_transform2/kis_tool_transform.cc b/plugins/tools/tool_transform2/kis_tool_transform.cc
index dbe9957..940c1fa 100644
--- a/plugins/tools/tool_transform2/kis_tool_transform.cc
+++ b/plugins/tools/tool_transform2/kis_tool_transform.cc
@@ -838,6 +838,11 @@ void KisToolTransform::activate(const QSet<KoShape*> &shapes)
                                       this, SLOT(slotMoveDiscreteRight()));
     m_actionConnections.addConnection(action("movetool-move-right-more"), SIGNAL(triggered(bool)),
                                       this, SLOT(slotMoveDiscreteRightMore()));
+    // Krita Nova: Ctrl+T while the Transform tool is already active (e.g.
+    // after applying or cancelling a transform) starts a new transform right
+    // away, instead of waiting for a click/tap on the canvas.
+    m_actionConnections.addConnection(action("KisToolTransform"), SIGNAL(triggered(bool)),
+                                      this, SLOT(slotToolActionRetriggered()));
     m_actionConnections.addConnection(action("increase_brush_size"),
                                       SIGNAL(triggered()),
                                       this,
@@ -855,6 +860,13 @@ void KisToolTransform::activate(const QSet<KoShape*> &shapes)
     nextActivationTransformMode = KisToolTransform::FreeTransformMode;
 }
 
+void KisToolTransform::slotToolActionRetriggered()
+{
+    if (m_strokeId || !image() || !currentNode()) return;
+    // same as clicking on the canvas with no transform running
+    startStroke(m_currentArgs.mode(), false);
+}
+
 void KisToolTransform::deactivate()
 {
     endStroke();
